{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794172095,"nonce":"eq03wJPqcBjc0gMXz/VnjvRwaYw=","title":"An issue carries a color, and a gantt group takes its head's","message":"An issue can carry a permanent color, opted into per type in the schema, and a gantt grouped by a relation draws each group in the color of the issue that heads it.\n\n## Design (for approval)\n\nAspects changed: `doc/design/schema.md`, `doc/design/views.md`, `doc/design/jira.md` (one rule), and `host/quickstart.md`.\n\n### A color is a kind (schema.md, new heading)\n\nA new field kind, `color`, joins the fixed list. Its value is one id out of a set fixed in code:\n`red`, `orange`, `green`, `cyan`, `blue`, `purple`, `magenta`, `gray`.\nA type opts in by declaring a field of that kind, `color: {kind: color, name: Color}`;\na type without one has no color, and a write of `color` to it is refused as any unknown field is.\nA `color` field takes no `values`, categories or `freeform`: the import refuses them, naming the fixed set.\nA write of any other value is refused naming the fixed set.\n\n- Not a built-in that a type switches on: the built-ins are the four fields every type has (schema.md, \"Built-ins are code\"), and a built-in that only some types have would be a fifth rule for what a type has.\n- Not an `enum` whose value ids happen to be color names: Go would have to read meaning into a configured value id, and a schema could spell `blue` as `bleu`, so no surface could draw it.\n- Not part of the set: `yellow`, because the gantt keeps it for the grabbed bar (views.md, \"Gantt groups are colors\"), so a grabbed bar always reads as grabbed.\n- Each id maps to one terminal color in `tui`, from the 256-color palette where the 16-color one lacks it (orange, purple).\n\n### The value is stored like any field's\n\nA color is an ordinary field value on the issue, so it replicates by push and pull, is set by `git work issue set ID '{\"color\":\"blue\"}'`, cleared by `null`, and read by `issue get`/`list` as the id string. `ordinal()` and `category()` are null on it.\n\n### The gantt takes a color field (views.md, \"Gantt groups are colors\", rewritten)\n\nA new optional gantt argument, `color`, names a field of kind `color` (No field roles: the flow passes the key, `work.view.gantt(..., group_by=\"parent\", color=\"color\")`). The argument check refuses a field that is not of kind `color` on some type.\nWhen `group_by` is a relation and `color` is given, a group's bars and header take the color the heading issue's `color` field holds; a group whose head holds none, or whose type lacks the field, takes the next palette color in the groups' order, as every group does today. With `group_by` on a non-relation field the argument changes nothing.\n- Not a row's own color too: a row's own color competing with its group's would make a group's bars two colors, which is what grouping by color is meant to avoid. (Can be a later issue.)\n\n### Show draws and edits it\n\nShow's fields table draws a color as its id in that color; `Space` edits it with the enum picker over the fixed set, `null` among them.\n\n### Jira never syncs a color (jira.md)\n\nA `color` field is local-only: `jira schema` never pairs it with a Jira field by name, and an import refuses `aliases: {jira: …}` on it other than `\"\"`. It is never on a pending or off-schema line, since only aliased fields are exported or imported. A test asserts a synced issue with a color set reports no pending and no off-schema item for it.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["issue-model","tui"],"status":"backlog","type":"story"}}]}